Read and obey `AGENTS.md` before any planning, code generation, edit, test, migration, PR, deployment, or completion claim.

The authoritative process is `docs/governance/TXKPRO_WAVE_IMPLEMENTATION_PROTOCOL.md`.

For "what's next", use `node scripts/roadmap-next-eligible.mjs --json`. Treat its result as provisional until all required read-only agent confirmations are resolved from authoritative sources. Continue context, dependency, source-review, preflight, confirmation resolution, and planning automatically in the same turn. Confirmation evidence must use `semantic-provenance-v3` with typed `assertion {subject,predicate,values}` plus machine-verifiable `verification`; generic proof text must contain the assertion subject and every asserted value. Include `implementationPlan.contract: sourced-plan-v1`; every API route, database field, status, event, URL pattern, credential, and owner must be SOURCED or labeled `PROPOSED — requires product/technical decision`. Read the canonical template/validator and reject semantic extrapolation. If a candidate fails confirmation, continue to the next provisional candidate. Never report mutation authorized before explicit owner approval.

For every implementation run, use `scripts/txkpro-agent-usage.mjs` to record the PRE-RUN estimate in the issue before mutation and POST-RUN actual usage before completion; never invent missing telemetry.

Use the repository's TXKPRO preflight, wave-manifest, protocol-check, and completion-report scripts. Never bypass evidence-gated Verification/Done transitions or the separate production-authorization gate.

Prose cannot upgrade runtime state. Only the exact armed validator invocation's structured `TXKPRO_CONFIRMATION_VALIDATION_RESULT` may clear the gate. Use the persisted validator-derived `ownerFacingResponse` exactly and never narratively upgrade `PROPOSED`, `BLOCKED`, or `UNRESOLVED`.
